msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Termālā starojuma joslas (Thermal Infra-Red)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 \"Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer (SLSTR)\" "
"instruments sniedz informāciju 2 specializētos kanālos (F1 un F2), kas "
"domāti virsmas temperatūras noteikšanai. F2 kanāls ar centrālo viļņa garumu "
"10854 nm veic mērījumus infrasarkanā spektra termālajā daļā (Thermal Infra "
"Red, TIR). Tas ir noderīgs ugunsgrēku monitoringa veikšanai. Dati pieejami "
"ar 1km horizontālo izšķirspēju.\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"### Methane (CH4)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Methane is, after carbon dioxide, the most important contributor to the "
"anthropogenically (caused by human activity) enhanced greenhouse effect. "
"Measurements are provided in parts per billion (ppb) with a spatial "
"resolution of 7 km x 3.5 km.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/tropomi-level-2-methane)"
msgstr ""
"### Metāns (CH4)\n"
"\n"
"Metāns ir viena no siltumnīcas efektu izraisošajām gāzēm, kas pastāv uz "
"Zemes un tās garozā un nokļūst atmosfērā cilvēka saimnieciskās darbības "
"dēļ. Mērījumi izteikti miljarda daļās (parts per billion, ppb) un pieejami "
"ar telpisko izķirtspēju 7 km x 3.5 km.\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/tropomi-level-2-methane)"

msgid ""
"### Formaldehyde (HCHO)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Long term satellite observations of tropospheric formaldehyde (HCHO) are "
"essential to support air quality and chemistry-climate related studies from "
"the regional to the global scale. The seasonal and inter-annual variations "
"of the formaldehyde distribution are principally related to temperature "
"changes and fire events, but also to changes in anthropogenic (human-made) "
"activities. Its lifetime being of the order of a few hours, HCHO "
"concentrations in the boundary layer can be directly related to the release "
"of short-lived hydrocarbons, which mostly cannot be observed directly from "
"space. Measurements are in mol per square meter (mol/ m^2).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-formaldehyde)"
msgstr ""
"### Farmaldehīds (HCHO)\n"
"\n"
"Ilgtermiņa satelītu novērojumi, kas nosaka farmaldehīda klātbūtni "
"troposfēra ir nozīmīgi pētījumos, kas saistīti ar gaisa kvalitāti un "
"ķīmisko sastāvu. Sezonālās un ilggadējās izmaiņas farmaldehīda izkliedē ir "
"saistītas ar gaisa temperatūras paaugstināšanos, meža ugunsgrēku "
"aktivitāti, kā arī cilvēka saimniecisko darbību. Šī gāze ātri nokļūst un "
"izkliedējas atmosfērā, tādēļ tālizpētes mērījumi ne vienmēr ir objektīvi. "
"Mērījumi izteikti molos uz kvadrātmetru (mol/m^2).\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-formaldehyde)"

msgid ""
"### Sulfur Dioxide (SO2)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Sulphur dioxide enters the Earth’s atmosphere through both natural and "
"anthropogenic (human made) processes. It plays a role in chemistry on a "
"local and global scale and its impact ranges from short term pollution to "
"effects on climate. Only about 30% of the emitted SO2 comes from natural "
"sources; the majority is of anthropogenic origin. Sentinel-5P/TROPOMI "
"instrument samples the Earth’s surface with a revisit time of one day with "
"a spatial resolution of 3.5 x 7 km which allows the resolution of fine "
"details including the detection of smaller SO2 plumes. Measurements are in "
"mol per square meter (mol/ m^2).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-sulphur-dioxide)"
msgstr ""
"### Sēra dioksīds (SO2)\n"
"\n"
"Sēra dioksīds nokļūst atmosfērā gan dabisko procesu, gan cilvēka "
"saimnieciskās darbības rezultātā. Tas būtiski ietekmē atmosfēras ķīmisko "
"sastāvu gan vietējā, gan globālā mērogā, un ir novērtējams gan kā īslaicīgs "
"piesārņojums, gan kā ilgtermiņa faktors, kas ietekmē klimatu. Tikai trešā "
"daļa no Sēra dioksīda piesārņojuma veidojas dabisko procesu rezultātā. "
"Sentinel-5P/TROPOMI instruments veic mērījumus reizi dienā ar telpisko "
"izšķirtspēju 3.5 x 7 km, tādējādi ļaujot veikt detalizētus novērojumus. "
"Mērījumi ir izteikti molos uz kvadrātmetru (mol/m^2).\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-sulphur-dioxide)"

msgid ""
"### Ozone (O3)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Ozone is of crucial importance for the equilibrium of the Earth atmosphere. "
"In the stratosphere, the ozone layer shields the biosphere from dangerous "
"solar ultraviolet radiation. In the troposphere, it acts as an efficient "
"cleansing agent, but at high concentration it also becomes harmful to the "
"health of humans, animals, and vegetation. Ozone is also an important "
"greenhouse-gas contributor to ongoing climate change. Since the discovery "
"of the Antarctic ozone hole in the 1980s and the subsequent Montreal "
"Protocol regulating the production of chlorine-containing ozone-depleting "
"substances, ozone has been routinely monitored from the ground and from "
"space. Measurements are in mol per square meter (mol/ m^2)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-ozone-profile)"
msgstr ""
"### Ozons (O3)\n"
"\n"
"Ozons ir gāzveida savienojums, kuram ir izšķiroša nozīme veidojot līdzsvaru "
"Zemes atmosfērā. Ozona slānis stratosfērā kalpo kā vairogs, kas pasargā "
"biosfēru no saules ultravioletā starojumu. Troposfērā esošais ozons "
"darbojas kā attīrošs līdzeklis, tomēr paaugstinātā koncentrācija tas paliek "
"kaitīgs dzīvajām būtnēm un augiem. Izmaiņas ozona daudzumā ir saistītas ar "
"klimata pārmaiņām. 1980. gados tika ievērots liela izmēra caurums virs "
"Antarktikas esošajā ozona slānī un kopš Montreālas protokla izveides ozona "
"monitorings tiek veikts gan uz zemes, gan izmantojot tālizpētes rīkus. "
"Mērījumi ir izteikti molos uz kvadrātmetru (mol/m^2).\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-ozone-profile)"

msgid ""
"### Nitrogen Dioxide (NO2)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Nitrogen dioxide (NO2) and nitrogen oxide (NO) together are usually "
"referred to as nitrogen oxides. They are important trace gases in the "
"Earth’s atmosphere, present in both the troposphere and the stratosphere. "
"They enter the atmosphere as a result of anthropogenic activities "
"(particularly fossil fuel combustion and biomass burning) and natural "
"processes (such as microbiological processes in soils, wildfires and "
"lightning). Measurements are in mol per square meter (mol/ m^2).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-nitrogen-"
"dioxide)"
msgstr ""
"### Slāpekļa dioksīds (NO2)\n"
"\n"
"Slāpekļa dioksīds un slāpekļa oksīds, jeb slāpekļa oksīdi ir nozīmīgi "
"gāzveida savienojumi Zemes atmosfērā. Tie ir sastopami gan troposfērā, gan "
"stratosfērā un rodas cilvēka saimnieciskās aktivitātes (fosilie enerģijas "
"avoti) un dabisko procesu (augsnes procesi, meža ugunsgrēki un zibens "
"izlādes) rezultātā. Mērījumi ir izteikti molos uz kvadrātmetru (mol/m^2).\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-nitrogen-"
"dioxide)"

msgid ""
"### Carbon Monoxide (CO)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Carbon monoxide (CO) is an important atmospheric trace gas. In certain "
"urban areas, it is a major atmospheric pollutant. Main sources of CO are "
"combustion of fossil fuels, biomass burning, and atmospheric oxidation of "
"methane and other hydrocarbons. The carbon monoxide total column is "
"measured in mol per square meter (mol/ m^2).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-carbon-monoxide)"
msgstr ""
"### Oglekļa Monoksīds (CO)\n"
"\n"
"Oglekļa monoksīds ir nozīmīgs gāzveida savienojums, kas sastopams Zemes "
"atmosfērā. Tā nokļūšana atmosfērā ir galvenokārt saistīta ar fosilo "
"enerģijas avotu patēriņu, degšanas procesiem, kā arī mijiedarbojoties ar "
"ogļūdeņraža savienojumiem. Mērījumi ir izteikti molos uz kvadrātmetru "
"(mol/m^2).\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-carbon-monoxide)"

msgid ""
"### Aerosol Index\n"
"\n"
"The Aerosol Index (AI) is a qualitative index indicating the presence of "
"elevated layers of aerosols in the atmosphere. It can be used to detect the "
"presence of UV absorbing aerosols such as desert dust and volcanic ash "
"plumes. Positive values (from light blue to red) indicate the presence of "
"UV-absorbing aerosol. This index is calculated for two pairs of "
"wavelengths: 340/380 nm and 354/388 nm.\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-ultraviolet-"
"aerosol-index)"
msgstr ""
"### Aerosolu Indekss (Aerosol Index, AI)\n"
"\n"
"Aerosolu Indekss (AI) ir kvantitatīvs index, kas norāda uz paaugstināta "
"aerosolu daudzumu atmosfērā. Indeksu var izmantot, lai noteiktu "
"Ultravioleto (UV) starojumu absorbējošus aerosolus, kā tuksneša putekļus "
"vai vulkānisko pelnu izmešus. Pozitīvas vērtības (gaiši zila līdz sarkana) "
"nordāda uz UV absorbējošu aerosolu klātbūtni. Šis indekss tiek aprēķināts 2 "
"satelītdatu kanālu pāriem - 340/380 nm un 354/388 nm.\n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit.](https://sentinels.copernicus.eu/web/sentinel/data-products/-/asset_"
"publisher/fp37fc19FN8F/content/sentinel-5-precursor-level-2-ultraviolet-"
"aerosol-index)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Mākoņu pamatnes augstums (Cloud base height)\n"
"\n"
"Mākoņu apakšējās robežas augstums metros (m)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Atmosfēras spiediens mākoņu pamatnē (Cloud base pressure)\n"
"\n"
"Spiediens mākoņa pamatnē, izteikts Paskālos (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Mākoņu optiskais biezums (Cloud optical thickness)\n"
"\n"
"Mākoņu biezuma parametrs ir viens no raksturlielumiem, kas tiek izmantots "
"mākoņu aprakstīšanai. Tas attaino saules gaismas(enerģijas) daudzu, kas "
"spēj šķērsot mākoni un nokļūt līdz Zemes virsmai. Jo lielāks ir mākoņa "
"biezums, jo lielāka daļa no saules enerģijas tiks izkliedēta un atstarota. "
"Tumši zilas vērtības norāda ir saistītas ar mazāku biezumu, bet sarkanā "
"krāsa norāda uz palielinātu biezumu."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Mākoņa virsotnes augstums (Cloud top height)\n"
"\n"
"Mākoņa augstākā robeža, izteikts metros (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Atmosfēras spiediens mākoņa virsotnē (Cloud top pressure)\n"
"\n"
"Spiediens mākoņa virsotnē, izteikts Paskālos (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Veģetācijas indekss ar atmosfēras korekciju (Atmospherically Resistant "
"Vegetation Index, ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Šis indekss samazina mērījuma traucējumus, kas saistīti ar saules gaismas "
"izkliedi atmosfērā. Tas ir īpaši noderīgs reģionos, kur atmosfērā ir "
"paaugstināts aerosolu daudzums (migla, putekļi, dūmi, gaisa piesārņojums). "
"Vērtības ir intervālā no -1 līdz 1. Veselīga veģetācija parasti ir ar "
"vērtībām no 0.20 līdz 0.80. \n"
"\n"
"Plašāka informācija "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) un "
"[šeit.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Uzlabotais Antocianīna Atstarošanās Indekss (Modified Anthocyanin "
"Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2))\n"
"\n"
"Antocianīns ir pigments, kas bieži sastopams augstākajos augos un ir "
"atbildīgs par to iekrāsošanu sarkanā, zilā un violetā tonī. Pigmenta "
"klātbūtnes noteikšana sniedz noderīgu infromāciju par augu veselību. "
"Antocianīna atstarošanās visizteiktāk novērojama elektromagnētsikā spektra "
"joslā ap 550 nm, tomēr šajā joslā novērojama arī hlorofila atstarošanās. "
"Lai atsevišķi izdalītu antocianīna klātbūtni tiek lietota 700 nm josla, kas "
"atstaro tikai hlorofilu un ļauj identificēt antocianīna klātbūtni 500 nm "
"joslā.\n"
"\n"
"Lai koriģētu signālu, kas saistīts ar blīvu un biezu lapotni tiek izmantots "
"tuvā infrasarkanā spektra josla (rekomendējoši tie ir 760-800 nm), kas ir "
"saistāma ar lapu radītu enerģijas izkliedi. \n"
"\n"
"Uzlabotais Antocianīna Atstarošanās Indekss (mARI/ARI2) ir plašāk "
"aprakstīts  [šajā oriģinālrakstā] "
"(https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/), kur novērotās "
"vērtības ir diapazonā no 0 līdz 8.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Zaļās Pilsētas Skripts (Green City Script)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins ir noderīgs zaļo zonu identificēšanai pilsētvidē. Tas izmanto "
"Veģetācijas Indeksu (NDVI) un informāciju no kanāliem (joslām), kas "
"saistīti ar redzamo gaismu. Apbūvēti apgabali ir redzami pelēkā krāsā, bet "
"zaļā krāsā redzami apgabli ar augāju.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Pilsētvides klasifikācijas Indekss (Urban Classified Script)\n"
"\n"
"Indekss paredzēts apbūvētu platību atpazīšanai, nošķirot augāju, ūdeni un "
"neizmantotu zemes virsmu. Platības ar augstu mitruma saturu ir redzamas "
"zilā krāsā, apbūvētas platības redzamas baltā krāsā, augājs redzams zaļā "
"krāsā, un neizmantotas zemes virsmas platības redzamas brūnā krāsā.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Pilsētvides skripts (Urban Land Infrared Color Script)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins, kuru veidojis Leo Tolari, apvieno dabisko krāsu vizualizāciju "
"ar datiem no īsviļņu(SWIR) un tuvajiem(NIR) infrasarkanajiem kanāliem. \n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Mitruma trūkums (NDMI for Moisture Stress)\n"
"\n"
"NDMI dati var tikt izmantoti lai atpazītu apūdeņošanas sistēmu klātbūtni un "
"to efektivitāti. Zinot zemes lietojuma un pārklājuma veidus ir iespējams "
"noteikt vai apgabals tiek apūdeņots. Zinot lauksaimniecības kultūru, kas "
"tiek audzēta ir iespējams novērtēt apūdeņošanas efektivitāti vasaras "
"veģetācijas periodā. Papildus tam, šo informāciju var lietot, lai "
"identificētu lauku apgabalus, kur apūdeņošana ir pārspīlēta vai "
"nepietiekama.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Mitruma Indekss (Normalized Difference Moisture Index, NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Indekss ir piemērots postoša sausuma monitoringam, kā arī lai noteiktu "
"augāja ūdens saturu. Vērtības ir intervālā no -1 līdz 1. Negatīvas vērtības "
"(tuvojas -1) norāda uz neapaugušiem zemes apgabaliem. Vērtības ap nulli "
"(-0.2 līdz 0.4) norāda uz ūdens trūkstošu ūdens apjomu (water stress). "
"Augstas, pozitīvas vērtības norāda uz augāju, kas neizjūt ūdens trūkumu "
"(0.4 līdz 1).\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Ūdens Indekss (Normalized Difference Water Index, NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Indekss ir piemērots ūdens tilpņu kartēšanai. Ūdens tilpņu vērtības ir "
"lielākas par 0.5, bet zemākas vērtības parasti sastītas ar veģetācijas "
"klātbūtni. Apbūvētas platības parasti ir ar vērtībām intervālā no 0 līdz "
"0.2.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum . Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. True color composite uses visible light bands red, green and blue in "
"the corresponding red, green and blue color channels, resulting in a "
"natural colored product, that is a good representation of the Earth as "
"humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"
msgstr ""
"# Dabiskā krāsojuma kompozītattēls (True Color composite)\n"
"\n"
"Sensori, kas veic zemes monitoringu iegūst informāciju par atstaroto "
"enerģiju dažādās elektromagnētiskā spektra daļās. Katra no šīm daļām tiek "
"dēvēta par kanālu, jeb joslu. Dabiskā krāsojuma attēls izmanto datus no "
"sarkanā, zaļā un zilā kanāla, tādējādi ļaujot attēlot Zemes virsmu, kas "
"līdzvērtīgs tam kādu to redzētu cilvēka acs.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-olci/"
"overview/heritage)"

msgid ""
"# Snow Classifier\n"
"\n"
"The Snow Classifier algorithm aims to detect snow by classifying pixels "
"based on different brightness and Normalized Difference Snow Index (NDSI) "
"thresholds. Values classified as snow are returned in bright vivid blue. "
"The script can overestimate snow areas over clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"
msgstr ""
"# Sniega klasifikators (Snow Classifier)\n"
"\n"
"Algoritms atpazīst ar sniegu klātus apgabalus, veicot pikseļu spožuma "
"klasificēšanu un izmantojot Sniega Indeksa (NDSI) robežvērtības. Vērtības, "
"kas saistītas ar sniega klātiem apgabliem ir koši zilas. Aprēķins var būt "
"kļūdains mākoņainos apstākļos.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/snow_classifier/)"

msgid ""
"# Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer (UWQV)\n"
"\n"
"The script aims to dynamically visualise the chlorophyll and sediment "
"conditions of water bodies, which are primary indicators of water quality. "
"The chlorophyll content ranges in colors from dark blue (low chlorophyll "
"content) through green to red (high chlorophyll content). Sediment "
"concentrations are colored brown; opaque brown indicates high sediment "
"content.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"
msgstr ""
"# Ulyssys Ūdens Kvalitātes Vizualizācija (Ulyssys Water Quality Viewer "
"(UWQV))\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins domāts, lai dinamiski ilustrētu hlorofila un nogulumu "
"klātbūtni ūdenstilpnēs, kas ir primārie ūdens kvalitātes indikatori. "
"Hloriofila saturs redzams krāsojumā no tumši zila(zems saturs), līdz zaļam "
"un sarkanam (augsts saturs). Nogulumu suspensija attēlota brūnos toņos, kur "
"tumša, necaurspīdīga krāsa norāda uz augstu suspensijas blīvumu.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ulyssys_water_"
"quality_viewer/)"

msgid ""
"# Highlight Optimized Natural Color\n"
"\n"
"This script aims to display the Earth in beautiful natural color images. It "
"uses highlight optimization to avoid burnt out pixels and to even out the "
"exposure.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Optimizēts Dabiskā krāsojuma attēls (Highlight Optimized Natural Color)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins domāts, lai attēlotu Zemes virsmas iezīmes to dabiskajās "
"krāsās. Aprēķins ņem vērā pikseļu vērtību diapazonu, lai izvairītos no "
"pārlieku spožu pikseļu attēlošanas. \n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://sentinel-hub.github.io/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/highlight_"
"optimized_natural_color/#)"

msgid ""
"# Geology 12, 8, 2 composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses short-wave infrared (SWIR) band 12 to differentiate "
"among different rock types (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). Each rock "
"and mineral type reflects short-wave infrared light differently, making it "
"possible to map out geology by comparing reflected SWIR light. Near "
"infrared (NIR) band 8 highlights vegetation and band 2 detects moisture, "
"both contributing to differentiation of ground materials. The composite is "
"useful for finding geological formations and features (e.g. faults, "
"fractures), lithology (e.g. granite, basalt, etc.) and mining applications.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"
msgstr ""
"# Ģeoloģiskās īpašības (Kanālu 12, 8, 2 kompozītattēls)\n"
"\n"
"Šī kanālu kombinācija izmanto īsviļņu infrasarkano kanālu 12 (SWIR), lai "
"izdalītu dažādus iežu tipus. Katrs iežu un minerālu tips ir ar specifisku "
"infrasarkanās enerģijas atsarošanas raksturinformāciju, tādējādi kanāla 12 "
"(SWIR) datus var izmantot, lai veiktu vispārēju ģeoloģisko kartēšanu. "
"Atstarošanās apjoms tuvajā infrasarkanajā (NIR) kanālā 8 izceļ augāju, bet "
"redzamās gaismas kanāls 2 palīdz noteikt mitruma atšķirības. Šī "
"kompozītattēla informācija ir noderīga meklējot ģeoloģiskus "
"veidojumus(piemēram, lūzumus), izdalot litoloģiju (granīts, bazalts, "
"utml.), kā arī kartējot derīgos izrakteņus.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk infromācijas "
"[šeit.](https://www.euspaceimaging.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/EUSI-SWIR."
"pdf)"

msgid ""
"# Wildfires\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, visualizes wildfires using "
"Sentinel-2 data. It combines natural color background with some NIR/SWIR "
"data for smoke penetration and more detail, while adding highlights from "
"B11 and B12 to show fires in red and orange colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"
msgstr ""
"# Meža ugunsgrēki (Wildfires)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins, kuru izveidojis Pierre Markuse, attēlo meža ugunsgrēkus "
"izmantojot Sentinel-2 datus. Dabiskā krāsojuma attēls tiek papildināts ar "
"NIW/SWIR datiem, lai iegūtu papildus detaļas. Atklāta liesma un ļoti "
"karstas virsmas ir izceltas ar sarkanu un oranžu krāsojumu.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/custom-scripts/sentinel-2/"
"markuse_fire/)"

msgid ""
"# Enhanced True Color\n"
"\n"
"This script, created by Pierre Markuse, uses multiple bands (a band is a "
"region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth "
"in different bands) and saturation and brightness control to enhance the "
"true color visualization.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"
msgstr ""
"# Uzlabotais dabiskā krāsojuma attēls (Enhanced True Color)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins, kuru izveidojis Pierre Markuse, izmanto datus no vairākām "
"elektromagnētiskā spektra joslām, kā arī veic krāsu spilgtuma un košuma "
"korekciju, lai uzlabotu dabiskā krāsojuma vizualizāciju. \n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/enhanced_true_"
"color-2/#)"

msgid ""
"# Burned Area Index\n"
"\n"
"Burned Area Index takes advantage of the wider spectrum of Visible, "
"Red-Edge, NIR and SWIR bands.\n"
"\n"
"Values description:()=> The range of values for the index is `-1` to `1` "
"for burn scars, and `1` - `6` for active fires. Different fire intensities "
"may result in different thresholds; the current values were calibrated, as "
"per original author, on mostly Mediterranen regions.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"
msgstr ""
"# Izdegušo Platību Indekss (Burned Area Index)\n"
"\n"
"Izdegušo Platību Indekss raksturo izdegušas zemes platības, izmantojot "
"datus no vairākām joslām elektromagnētiskajā spektrā. \n"
"\n"
"Vērtību diapazona apraksts:()=> Izdegušas platības ir ar vērtībām no -1 "
"līdz 1, bet aktīvas liesmas redzamas ar vērtībām no 1 līdz 6. Liesmas "
"intensitātes izmaiņas var radīt atsķirības robežvērtību diapazonā. Šeit "
"piedāvātās robežvertības ir kalibrētas Vidusjūras reģionā un to veicis "
"aprēķina autors.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/bais2/)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospheric penetration\n"
"\n"
"This composite uses different bands (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands) in the non-visible part of the electromagnetic spectrum to reduce "
"the influence of the atmosphere in the image. Short wave infrared bands 11 "
"and 12 are highly reflected by the heated areas, making them useful for "
"fire and burned area mapping. Near infrared band 8, is on contrary, highly "
"reflected by vegetation, which signifies absence of fire. Vegetation "
"appears blue, displaying details related to the vegetation vigor. Healthy "
"vegetation is shown in light blue while the stressed, sparse or/and arid "
"vegetation appears in dull blue. Urban features are white, grey, cyan or "
"purple.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmosfēras caursite (Atmospheric penetration)\n"
"\n"
"Šis kompozītattēls ir veidots izmantojot dažādus kanālus (joslas) "
"neredzamajā gaismas spektra daļā. Tā nolūluks ir novērst ietekmi uz "
"signālu, kuru veido atmosfēra. Īsviļņu infraskarkanajā spektra daļā(SWIR "
"kanāli 11 un 12) izceļas virsmas ar paaugstinātu  temperatūru, kas ir "
"noderīgi kartējot aktīvus ugunsgrēkus un izdegušas platības. Signāls no "
"kanāla 8 (NIR) izceļ veselīgu augāju. Augājs redzams zilos toņos, atkarībā "
"no mitruma un blīvuma. Pilsētvides objekti ir baltā, pelēkā un/vai violetā "
"krāsā.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk infromācijas [šeit.]https://eos.com/atmospheric-penetration/)"

msgid ""
"# Barren Soil Visualization\n"
"\n"
"The Barren Soil Visualization can be useful for soil mapping, to "
"investigate the location of landslides or the extent of erosion in "
"non-vegetated areas. This visualization shows all vegetation in green and "
"the barren ground in red. Water appears black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) and "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"
msgstr ""
"# Neproduktīvo augšņu vizualizācija (Barren Soil Visualization)\n"
"\n"
"Šis kompozītattēls ir noderīgs augšņu kartēšanai, lai pētītu zemes "
"noslīdeņus vai erozijas apmērus apgabalos, kur nav veģetācijas. "
"Vizualizācija izceļ augāju zaļā un augsni sarkanā krāsā. Ūdens tiek "
"attēlots melnā krāsā.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk infromācijas "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/barren_soil/) un "
"[šeit.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/create-useful-and-beautiful-"
"satellite-images-with-custom-scripts-8ef0e6a474c6)"

msgid ""
"# True Color with IR Highlights composite\n"
"\n"
"This composite enhances the true color visualization by adding the "
"shortwave infrared wavelengths to amplify details. It displays heated areas "
"in red/orange.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"
msgstr ""
"# Patiesā krāsojuma un infrasarkanā signāla kompozītattēls\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins uzlabo patieso krāsu vizualizāciju, papildinot to ar "
"informāciju no īsviļņu infrasarkanās gaismas spektra daļas. Sakarsētas "
"virsmas tiek izceltas ar sarkanu/oranžu krāsojumu.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://medium.com/sentinel-hub/active-volcanoes-as-seen-from-space-"
"9d1de0133733)"

msgid ""
"# Detection of Burned Areas\n"
"\n"
"This script is used to detect large scale recently burned areas. Pixels "
"colored red highlight burned areas, and all other pixels are returned in "
"true color. The script sometimes overestimates burned areas over water and "
"clouds.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"
msgstr ""
"# Izdegušo platību noteikšana (Detection of Burned Areas)\n"
"\n"
"Šis aprēķins ir lietojams nesen degušu zemes platību identificēšanai. "
"Sarkanā krāsā izceltas izdegušas platības, kamēr pārējā zemes virsma tiek "
"attēlota dabiskajā krāsojumā.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/burned_area_ms/)"

msgid ""
"# Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index (OTCI) is estimated based on the "
"chlorophyll content in terrestrial vegetation and can be used to monitor "
"vegetation condition and health. Low OTCI values usually signify water, "
"sand or snow. Extremely high values, displayed with white, usually suggest "
"the absence of chlorophyll as well. They generally represent either bare "
"ground, rock or clouds. The chlorophyll values in between range from red "
"(low chlorophyll values) to dark green (high chlorophyll values) can be "
"used to determine vegetation health.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"
msgstr ""
"# Sauszemes Hlorofila Indekss (Terrestrial Chlorophyll Index, OTCI)\n"
"\n"
"OTCI tiek aprēķināts sekojot sauszemes augāja hlorofila saturam. Idekss "
"tiek izmantots augāja veselīguma un stāvokļa monitoringam. Zemas vērtības "
"parasti saistītas ar ūdens, smilšu vai sniega pārklājumu. Ekstremāli "
"augstas vērtības (redzamas baltā krāsā) var norādīt uz hlorofila neesamību "
"- piemēram atklātas, neauglīgas sauszemes virsmas, ieži vai mākoņi. "
"Hlorofila vērtības intervālā no sarkanas (zems) līdz zaļai (augstss) var "
"tikt izmantotas nosakot augāja veselīgumu.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-3/otci/)"

msgid "Create a timelapse of this area"
msgstr "Veidot attēlu animāciju šim reģionam"

