msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Augsnei pielāgotais veģetācijas indekss (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Augsnei pielāgotais veģetācijas indekss ir līdzīgs normalizētajam "
"diferenciālajam veģetācijas indeksam (NDVI), taču to izmanto apgabalos ar "
"nelielu veģetācijas segumu (< 40%). Indekss ir transformācijas paņēmiens, "
"kas samazina augsnes spilgtuma ietekmi spektrālajos veģetācijas indeksos, "
"kuros izmanto sarkano un tuvo infrasarkano (NIR) viļņu garumu. Indekss ir "
"noderīgs, analizējot jaunas kultūras, sausus reģionus ar retu augāju un "
"atklātas augsnes virsmas.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) un "
"[šeit.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The Sentinel-2 normalised difference snow index can be used to "
"differentiate between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the "
"short-wave infrared light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is "
"generally reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in "
"bright vivid blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Sniega Indekss (Normalized Difference Snow Index, NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-2 sniega indekss ir noderīgs, lai atšķirtu mākoņus no sniega "
"klātām virsmām. Sniega virsmas absorbē enerģiju īsviļņu infrasarkanajā "
"spektra daļā un atstaro enerģiju redzamās gaismas spektra daļā, turpretim "
"mākoņiem ir augsta atstarojamība abās šajās elektromagnētiskā spektra "
"daļās. Sniega klātas virsmas redzamas spilgti zilā krāsā.\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

