msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Termālais kanāls 10\n"
"\n"
"Šī termālā vizualizācija ir balstīta uz 10. kanālu (kanāls ir "
"elektromagnētiskā spektra apgabals; satelīta sensors var attēlot Zemi "
"dažādos kanālos). Ar centrālo viļņa garumu 10895 nm tas mēra termālajā "
"infrasarkanajā diapazonā jeb TIR. Tā vietā, lai mērītu gaisa temperatūru kā "
"meteoroloģiskās stacijas, 10. kanāls atspoguļo pašu zemes virsmu, kas bieži "
"ir daudz karstāka. Termālais kanāls 10 ir noderīgs virsmas temperatūru "
"iegūšanai, un tā dati tiek vākti ar 100 metru izšķirtspēju.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# True color composite\n"
"\n"
"Sensors carried by satellites can image Earth in different regions of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum. Each region in the spectrum is referred to as a "
"band. Landsat 8-9 has 11 bands. True color composite uses visible light "
"bands red, green and blue in the corresponding red, green and blue color "
"channels, resulting in a natural colored product, that is a good "
"representation of the Earth as humans would see it naturally.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."
msgstr ""
"# Dabisko krāsu salikums\n"
"\n"
"Satelītu nesētie sensori var attēlot Zemi dažādos elektromagnētiskā spektra "
"apgabalos. Katru spektra apgabalu sauc par kanālu. Landsat 8-9 ir 11 "
"kanāli. Dabisko krāsu salikums izmanto redzamās gaismas sarkano, zaļo un "
"zilo kanālu attiecīgi sarkanajā, zaļajā un zilajā krāsu kanālā, iegūstot "
"dabiskās krāsās attēlotu produktu, kas labi atspoguļo Zemi tā, kā cilvēks "
"to redzētu dabiski.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/landsat-8/composites/)."

msgid ""
"# Pansharpened True Color\n"
"\n"
"The pansharpened true color composite is done by using the usual true color "
"data (red, green and blue (RGB)) and enhancing them by using the "
"panchromatic band 8, or pan band (a band is a region of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). An image "
"from the pan band is similar to black-and-white film: it combines light "
"from the red, green, and blue parts of the spectrum into a single measure "
"of overall visible reflectance. Pansharpened images have 4x the resolution "
"of the usual true color composite, greatly enhancing the usefulness of "
"Landsat imagery.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."
msgstr ""
"# Ar pankromātisko kanālu asinātas dabiskās krāsas\n"
"\n"
"Ar pankromātisko kanālu asināto dabisko krāsu salikumu iegūst, izmantojot "
"parastos dabisko krāsu datus (sarkano, zaļo un zilo (RGB)) un uzlabojot tos "
"ar pankromātisko 8. kanālu jeb pan kanālu (kanāls ir elektromagnētiskā "
"spektra apgabals; satelīta sensors var attēlot Zemi dažādos kanālos). Pan "
"kanāla attēls ir līdzīgs melnbaltai filmai: tas apvieno gaismu no spektra "
"sarkanās, zaļās un zilās daļas vienā kopējās redzamās atstarošanas "
"mērījumā. Ar pankromātisko kanālu asinātajiem attēliem ir 4 reizes lielāka "
"izšķirtspēja nekā parastajam dabisko krāsu salikumam, kas ievērojami "
"palielina Landsat attēlu lietderību.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://blog.mapbox.com/pansharpening-for-higher-resolution-in-"
"landsat-live-e4717cd7c356)."

msgid ""
"# Normalised Difference Snow Index (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalised difference snow index (NDSI) can be used to differentiate "
"between cloud and snow cover as snow absorbs in the short-wave infrared "
"light, but reflects the visible light, whereas cloud is generally "
"reflective in both wavelengths. Snow cover is represented in bright vivid "
"blue.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalizētais diferenciālais sniega indekss (NDSI)\n"
"\n"
"Normalizēto diferenciālo sniega indeksu (NDSI) var izmantot, lai atšķirtu "
"mākoņus no sniega seguma, jo sniegs absorbē īsviļņu infrasarkano gaismu, "
"bet atstaro redzamo gaismu, savukārt mākoņi parasti atstaro abos viļņu "
"garumos. Sniega segums tiek attēlots spilgti zilā krāsā.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Vairāk informācijas "
"[šeit](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndsi/)."

msgid ""
"The **Landsat 8-9** collection contains imagery from the two most recently "
"launched Landsat satellites (Landsat 8 and Landsat 9, provided by "
"NASA/USGS). Both carry the Operational Land Imager (OLI) and the Thermal "
"Infrared Sensor (TIRS), with 9 optical and 2 thermal bands. These two "
"sensors provide seasonal coverage of the global landmass.\n"
"\n"
"**Spatial resolution:** 15 m for the panchromatic band and 30 m for the "
"rest (the thermal bands are re-sampled from 100 m).\n"
"\n"
"**Revisit time:** 16 days\n"
"\n"
"**Data availability:** Since January 2021\n"
"\n"
"**Common usage:** Vegetation monitoring, land use, land cover maps, change "
"monitoring, etc.\n"
"\n"
"**Level-1** data (from **Landsat Collection 2**) provides global top of the "
"atmosphere reflectance and top of the atmosphere brightness temperature "
"products. \n"
"  \n"
"The data underwent several processing steps including geometric and "
"radiometric improvements. \n"
"  \n"
"More info about Level-1 data "
"[here](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/APIs/SentinelHub/Data/"
"Landsat8-9.html)."
msgstr ""
"**Landsat 8-9** kolekcija satur attēlus no diviem pēdējiem palaistajiem "
"Landsat satelītiem (Landsat 8 un Landsat 9, ko nodrošina NASA/USGS). Abi "
"nes Operational Land Imager (OLI) un Thermal Infrared Sensor (TIRS) ar 9 "
"optiskajiem un 2 termālajiem kanāliem. Šie divi sensori nodrošina sezonālu "
"globālās sauszemes aptveri.\n"
"\n"
"**Telpiskā izšķirtspēja:** 15 m pankromātiskajam kanālam un 30 m pārējiem "
"(termālie kanāli tiek pārsamplēti no 100 m).\n"
"\n"
"**Atkārtota apmeklējuma laiks:** 16 dienas\n"
"\n"
"**Datu pieejamība:** Kopš 2021. gada janvāra\n"
"\n"
"**Biežākais pielietojums:** Augāja monitorings, zemes izmantošanas un zemes "
"seguma kartes, izmaiņu monitorings u. c.\n"
"\n"
"**1. līmeņa** dati (no **Landsat Collection 2**) nodrošina globālus "
"atmosfēras augšējās robežas atstarošanas un atmosfēras augšējās robežas "
"radiometriskās temperatūras produktus. \n"
"  \n"
"Dati ir izgājuši vairākus apstrādes soļus, tostarp ģeometriskus un "
"radiometriskus uzlabojumus. \n"
"  \n"
"Vairāk informācijas par 1. līmeņa datiem "
"[šeit](https://documentation.dataspace.copernicus.eu/APIs/SentinelHub/Data/"
"Landsat8-9.html)."

msgid "NDVI 300m 10-daily V3"
msgstr "NDVI 300m 10-daily V3"

msgid ""
"Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) is an indicator of the "
"greenness of the biomes. Every 10-days estimates are available at global "
"scale in the spatial resolution of about 300 m from 2014 to June 2020. More "
"information "
"[here](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/vegetation/normalized-"
"difference-vegetation-index-300m-v1.0)."
msgstr ""
"Normalizētais diferenciālais veģetācijas indekss (NDVI) ir biomu zaļuma "
"rādītājs. Ik pēc 10 dienām aprēķini ir pieejami globālā mērogā ar aptuveni "
"300 m telpisko izšķirtspēju no 2014. gada līdz 2020. gada jūnijam. Vairāk "
"informācijas "
"[šeit](https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/vegetation/normalized-"
"difference-vegetation-index-300m-v1.0)."

